A||||7||Master_Sushi||84-4.10 Trans Oil Change||||3||
Z||000000||Master_Sushi||11-01-2001||07:18 PM||||I have an 84SE thats just about to hit 100K miles. I would like to change the transmission oil because its probably past due, but I dont know how  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">. I looked around and can't find any drain plugs or even an area to check and fill the oil. Im not having any problums with my trans now, I just want to keep it fresh!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Basicly...<BR>How do I check the oil in the 84 4.10 4 speed?<P>How would I go about changing it?<P>Should I just use a quality 5w-30, would using Mobil 1 be ok??<P>I looked up in my chiltons and it said it takes 5qts. Is this true?<P>Any other tips or tricks would be helpfull. I never have changed transmission oil. I have done just about everything else to my fiero though  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">.<P>As allways-Thanks for any input!||||reg||3
Z||000001||samoht||11-01-2001||07:25 PM||||you are joking right ???  You better just take it to a trans shop||||reg||1
Z||000002||Master_Sushi||11-01-2001||09:01 PM||||Its not possable to change it by myself then? I didn't know this, I thought I could change it. Im not exactly a newbie to automotive work, but im not an expert either. Has anyone done this before???||||reg||11
Z||000003||MooCow||11-01-2001||09:05 PM||||I have a 4:10 in my car with my 3.4 and I am pretty sure that there is a screw at the bottom area of the tranny.  I am going to be replacing mine cause it has an 8 inch crack in it.  But I remember there being a screw at the bottom of the tranny and I think that is the drain hole.  Similar to how you change your oil.<P>Thanks Ken||||reg||1
Z||000004||Master_Sushi||11-02-2001||11:13 AM||||Right... Nobody knows anything else???<P>Is it a stupid question or something?<P>||||reg||4
Z||000005||Banzai||11-02-2001||11:21 AM||||There is a drain plug similar to the one on your oil pan at the bottom of the tranny. Warm up the tranny by driving the car for about 10 miles. Drain the oil. You can pull the VSS(Vehicle Speed Sensor) out of the top to fill. It takes 3.5 quarts, NOT FIVE!!!!!!.  There is also a fill plug on the side of the tranny(it has a plastic tab with 5W-30 Only printed on it). Take this plug out. Buy a 4qt jug of Mobil 1 5W-30. Fill the tranny through the VSS hole until oil stars to come out the fill hole on the side of the tranny. Put a dab of silicone on the bottom of the drain plug bolt head, reinstall. Reinstall the fill plug and the VSS. Happy Shifting!<P>Banzai !!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000006||Rodrv6||11-02-2001||04:06 PM||||Just like Banzai said with one caution:  Be careful when you pull the VSS out of the case so the speedometer gear doesn't fall off the shaft and get lost in the case.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  <BR>White 88 GT :)||||reg||1
Z||000007||William Federle||11-02-2001||06:40 PM||||I've got a 1984 SE with a 4 speed. I drained the oil out the bottom - there's a drain plug there. On the driver's side of the transmission toward the rear of the transmission, in the upper half, there's a fill plug. Mine had a plastic placard on it saying something about using 5W30. I used a hose and the cut-off end of a turkey baster to get the oil in it. I used a funnel at the top of the hose. <P>I've read more than one horror story about losing the gear off of the speed sensor. That would be my very last choice of a way to get oil back into the transmission.<P>||||reg||1
